{"message":"Yes. Since the Light Blue card ending in 6129 was permanently closed because of suspected fraud, it cannot be reactivated. You’ll need a replacement card to continue using that account’s debit-card services, and ordering one is recommended. Any recurring payments linked to the old card will need to be updated.

Your TechWorld dispute remains subject to the investigation. Because it was reported after the 2-business-day window but within 60 days, potential liability can be up to $500; since the dispute is $412.88, that could mean the full disputed amount. The $412.88 provisional credit has been issued while the bank investigates and could be reversed if the claim is denied.

If you’d like me to help order the replacement card, please choose a delivery option: standard (free, 7–10 business days), expedited ($15, 3–5 business days), or rush ($35, 1–2 business days)."}
